    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (86.62) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12). **Yordan Alvarez** is the clear daily ceiling play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez and a prime #2 slot, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our most essential asset for the SB category. His elite projection is bolstered by a +14% dynamic platoon edge and a +4% bonus for facing a slow-delivery pitcher, making him a prime candidate to maximize our speed efficiency. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (74.38) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) are locked in as high-floor, high-upside anchors, with **Christian Yelich** specifically capitalizing on a +10% boost for hitting out of the leadoff spot against Jose Cabrera.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary driver of our offensive strategy today, as **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) and **Carson Benge** (63.26) both see their value significantly inflated by favorable R/R matchups and top-of-the-order security. **Nelson Velazquez** (59.43) sits just inside the start threshold, buoyed by an elite 0.423 xwOBA and platoon advantage against David Peterson. The most difficult decision rested on **Caleb Durbin** (47.13), who finished as our top bench option; while his stolen base profile is intriguing, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher raw efficiency of the lower-order starters due to **Caleb Durbin** facing a tougher assignment in Reid Detmers. We are currently navigating \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board\u2014including for **Gary Sanchez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014so owners should monitor potential pinch-hit risks or lineup shuffles that could neutralize these projected advantages.",
